SUMMARY:[Machine Learning][Deep Representation Learning] LoG 2026 - Abstrac
 t registration deadline (both tracks)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: Learning on Graphs Conference\nWebsite: https
 ://logconference.org/\nSource URL: https://logconference.org/cfp/\nLocati
 on: Boston\, Massachusetts\, USA\nTopics: Machine Learning\, Deep Represe
 ntation Learning\, Complex Systems & Network Science\, Learning Theory & 
 Statistical Foundations\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based / non-arch
 ival extended abstracts\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-1
 0-07\nNotes: Fifth annual edition\, in person at Northeastern University.
  Extended Aug 5/7 deadlines replace the struck-through July 29/Aug 1 date
 s. Proceedings papers and non-archival extended abstracts share the regis
 tration and final submission cutoffs\, represented as one route. The TMLR
  presentation track requires an already published paper\, so it is not a 
 new-paper opportunity. LoG is distinct from LOD/AIS. Size M is an editori
 al estimate.\nScope: Learning on graphs and geometry: graph neural networ
 ks\, equivariant models\, graph kernels\, geometric and graph generative 
 models\, and statistical theory for structured data. Graph signal process
 ing\, causal graph models\, robustness\, and scalable graph-learning infr
 astructure are meaningful extensions. A graph or geometric contribution s
 hould remain central\, even in an application such as language or molecul
 ar modeling.\nAdditional topics: Probabilistic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\
 , Signal Processing\, Robustness & Safety\, ML Systems & Infrastructure\n
 Scope sources (2026): https://logconference.org/cfp/\nScope last checked:
  2026-10-07
URL:https://logconference.org/cfp/
END:VEVENT
